Show a task's full detail incl. tags/annotations/deps (maps to task.get)

Usage: tasqx show [OPTIONS] <REF>

Arguments:
  <REF>  short_id or UUID

Options:
      --card             Print the task as a 72-column box-drawn card, for pasting into a document
      --json             Print the raw JSON API result instead of the human table
      --ascii            With --card: draw the borders with + - | instead of box-drawing characters
      --theme <THEME>    Theme name (built-in nord|gruvbox|dracula|solarized|mono, or a user file). Overrides $TASQX_THEME and the config file (DESIGN.md §8)
      --socket <SOCKET>  Local socket / named-pipe address of a tasqx daemon. Overrides $TASQX_SOCK. When a daemon is reachable, one-shot commands route through it (single writer); otherwise they run in-process. Also selects the address for `daemon` and `watch`
      --no-daemon        Never route through a daemon; always run one-shot in-process (the pre-daemon behaviour). Escape hatch for scripts
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

EXAMPLES
  tasqx show 1
  tasqx show 1 --card

NOTE  Full detail: tags, annotations, dependencies, blocked state, `_rev`.
      `--card` prints a fixed 72-column box-drawn card meant to be pasted into a document (a chat, a PR); `--ascii` draws its borders with `+ - |`. The default screen is unchanged (D146).

See also: modify · why · annotate        Full manual: tasqx manual
